# Prefer `fn` over raw loops

Raw `for` loops over slices or maps that **build a collection** (map, filter, remap, fallible collect) are **forbidden** unless they match an allowlisted case below. Use **`github.com/zhulik/forma/fn`** (`Map`, `Filter`, `FilterMap`, `MapErr`, `FilterMapErr`, `MapValues`, `MapEntries`, …). Add a new exported helper in `fn/` when the pattern is useful—do not add third-party collection libraries. This exemption is deliberate under `prefer-reuse-over-handroll`: prefer reuse elsewhere, but **never** replace `fn/` with an external collection/util package.

Side-effect-only **each** walks (including fallible I/O that does not return a built collection) MAY use raw `for`.

## Allowlist (raw `for` OK)

1. Inside `fn/` — implementing helpers.
2. Generated code — `*.gen.go` and similar.
3. Table-driven tests — `for _, tc := range tests { t.Run(...) }`.
4. Side-effect-only each — walk a slice or map for writes, deletes, logging, etc.; purpose is not building a returned collection.
5. Non-slice / non-map iteration — channels, `select`, infinite loops; ranging a string for runes when needed.
6. Indexed count APIs — C-style `for i := 0; i < n; i++` when there is no slice to `range` (e.g. tree-sitter `NamedChildCount`).
7. Short-circuit search — early `return` / `break` that is not “accumulate a collection” (e.g. pick first match).
8. Index-heavy algorithms — need indices for pairing, two cursors, in-place swap (not merely “I wanted `i`”).

Fallible loops whose **purpose** is to build a slice or map MUST use `MapErr` / `FilterMapErr` (or map `*Err` helpers), even if the callback also does I/O.

## Do

- Use existing `fn` helpers when semantics match.
- Extend `fn` with a small, well-named function when no helper exists yet (callback style `func(T)` / `func(K, V)`, not index args).
- Pass a named function when the signature already matches—**no no-op proxy lambdas**:

```go
// BAD
fn.Map(items, func(item Item) JSON { return toJSON(item) })

// GOOD
fn.Map(items, toJSON)
```

## Examples

```go
// BAD — manual dedupe + filter
// ... append loop with seen map ...

// GOOD
names := fn.Uniq(fn.Filter(names, func(name string) bool { return name != "" }))
```

```go
// GOOD — fallible collect
widgets, err := fn.FilterMapErr(paths, analyzeOne)
```

```go
// GOOD — side-effect each (allowlisted)
for _, name := range stale {
	if err := os.Remove(path); err != nil {
		return err
	}
}
```

Authors dot-import `fn` in UI code; library and CLI code may use a normal import.
